# p12 asked, and the answer was "unknown" (contrast with p01)
#
# LinkML option: option1 or option2, with a reason value that must stay distinct from blank.
#
# INVENTED: an archive interviewer asked a witness how tall Napoleon was, and the witness answered
# that they did not know. That answer is data: a categorical measurement datum output by a survey
# administration assay, whose categorical value specification is typed NCIT:C79729 'Asked but
# Unknown' and carries the literal answer.
#
# Terms (template p12, checked 2026-09-14): no OBI, IAO, or GENEPIO term for "asked but unknown".
# NCIT:C79729 ("An indication that a question was asked and the response is unknown"). HL7 v3
# NullFlavor ASKU and FHIR data-absent-reason asked-unknown are code system codes, not per-code
# IRIs, so they appear as a literal. Typing a value specification with an NCIT answer class is
# this example's choice, not an OBI pattern.
#
# A consumer can infer that the question was asked and the witness could not answer, which is a
# finding about the witness's knowledge, not a gap in the record. They cannot infer the height,
# and must not count this record as missing data.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/napoleon/> .
@prefix RO:   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_> .
@prefix IAO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_> .
@prefix OBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .
@prefix NCIT: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_> .
@prefix NCBITaxon: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_> .

ex:witness1 a owl:NamedIndividual , NCBITaxon:9606 ;
    rdfs:label "witness 1 (invented)" .

ex:witnessInterview1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:0003725 ;
    rdfs:label "witness interview 1 (invented archive record)" ;
    RO:0000057 ex:witness1 ;
    OBI:0000299 ex:answerDatum1 .

ex:answerDatum1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:0000938 ;
    IAO:0000136 ex:napoleonHeight ;
    rdfs:comment "Answer to: how tall was he?" ;
    OBI:0001938 ex:answerValueSpec1 .

ex:answerValueSpec1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:0001930 , NCIT:C79729 ;
    OBI:0002135 "unknown (HL7 NullFlavor ASKU; FHIR data-absent-reason asked-unknown)" .
